<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    "The Claim"  -  v1 row 3.
    Spec: design/Jawa/worldbuilding/v1_quest_the_claim.md (a retired seat, 2026-08-13).
    Player-facing strings are a retired seat's, verbatim; nodes and amounts another's.

    No node class, field or defName below is guessed. Provenance, all under
    C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\RimWorld\Data :

      QuestScriptDef fields rootSelectionWeight, rootMinPoints, expireDaysRange,
      everAcceptableInSpace, defaultChallengeRating
        Core/Defs/QuestScriptDefs/Script_BanditCamp.xml lines 6-11
      QuestNode_Sequence, GetMap(canBeSpace), GetSiteTile(preferCloserTiles),
      ViolentQuestsAllowed, Set, GetSitePartDefsByTagsAndFaction,
      GetDefaultSitePartsParams, SubScript, SpawnWorldObjects,
      WorldObjectTimeout(isQuestTimeout, inSignalDisable), Letter, End
        Core/Defs/QuestScriptDefs/Script_ItemStash.xml
      QuestNode_SetItemStashContents, QuestNode_SignalActivable
        Royalty/Defs/QuestScriptDefs/Intro/Script_Intro_Deserter.xml lines 91-96, 160-166
      QuestNode_Letter at sequence top level with no inSignal  =  fires on accept
        Royalty/Defs/QuestScriptDefs/Scripts_Permits.xml line 79
      Util_AdjustPointsForDistantFight, Util_GenerateSite  (both Core)
        Core/Defs/QuestScriptDefs/Scripts_Utility_ThreatsCore.xml lines 152, 346
      ComponentSpacer, ComponentIndustrial
        Core/Defs/ThingDefs_Items/Items_Resource_Manufactured.xml lines 153, 123
      ChunkSlagSteel
        Core/Defs/ThingDefs_Misc/Various_Stone.xml line 105

    Core only. Royalty/Ideology/Biotech/Odyssey/Anomaly are referenced for
    PROVENANCE, never as a dependency: every def and class named in the body
    ships in Core, so a DLC or mod change cannot orphan this quest.

    Space layer, deliberate and copied from OpportunitySite_BanditCamp:
      everAcceptableInSpace  gates ACCEPTANCE by the player, not site placement.
                             Proof, not the field's name:
                             (a) Core/Languages/English/Keyed/MainTabs.xml line
                                 198 is QuestNotSpace, "cannot accept in space",
                                 sitting inside the block of quest ACCEPT
                                 requirement strings (QuestRequiredPlayerWealth,
                                 QuestAlliedTo, QuestRequiredLayer);
                             (b) the six Odyssey quests whose sites really are in
                                 orbit (Script_SpaceSites.xml) set this field
                                 ZERO times, while Script_TradeRequest.xml sets
                                 it true on line 10 and forces its target
                                 ground-only on line 49. The "site placement"
                                 reading is exactly inverted by both.
                             Core's ItemStash omits it, so vanilla's stash quest
                             is silently unacceptable aboard a ship. This is a
                             gravship campaign, so it is set true here.
      GetMap canBeSpace      gates WHICH player map becomes $map.
      GetSiteTile            gates SITE placement, and is ground layer by
                             default; Odyssey's orbital sites use
                             QuestNode_Root_Site canBeSpace instead. So the site
                             stays on the ground, as the spec requires, while the
                             offer still reaches a colony that is off the surface.

    The rival clan is a STORY FACT. No FactionDef is authored or referenced by it;
    it exists only to explain the timer.
  -->

  <QuestScriptDef>
    <defName>Jawa_TheClaim</defName>
    <rootSelectionWeight>1.0</rootSelectionWeight>
    <rootMinPoints>0</rootMinPoints>
    <defaultChallengeRating>1</defaultChallengeRating>
    <expireDaysRange>4~8</expireDaysRange>
    <everAcceptableInSpace>true</everAcceptableInSpace>

    <questNameRules>
      <rulesStrings>
        <li>questName->The Claim</li>
      </rulesStrings>
    </questNameRules>

    <questDescriptionRules>
      <rulesStrings>
        <li>questDescription->Something came down past the ridge two nights ago — big enough to see, far enough that nobody has walked out to it yet.\n\nNobody who will admit to it.\n\nClan law is old and short: the wreck belongs to whoever plants a marker on it. Not to whoever saw it, and not to whoever needs it. Whoever gets there.</li>
      </rulesStrings>
    </questDescriptionRules>

    <root Class="QuestNode_Sequence">
      <nodes>

        <li Class="QuestNode_SubScript">
          <def>Util_AdjustPointsForDistantFight</def>
        </li>

        <li Class="QuestNode_GetMap">
          <canBeSpace>true</canBeSpace>
        </li>

        <!-- Accepted beat. No inSignal, so this fires when the quest starts. -->
        <li Class="QuestNode_Letter">
          <label>The Claim</label>
          <text>The marker is cut and stowed. Now it is a walking problem.</text>
        </li>

        <!--
          The haul, fixed rather than rolled, so the reward rule is guaranteed
          instead of hoped for. Low end on purpose:
            1x ComponentSpacer     the one category the clan cannot make - it
                                   needs Advanced fabrication and a fabrication
                                   bench, neither of which v1 has.
            8x ComponentIndustrial the useful part of the haul.
            4x ChunkSlagSteel      the texture: stripped hull, smelts to steel.
        -->
        <li Class="QuestNode_SetItemStashContents">
          <items>
            <li>ComponentSpacer</li>
            <li>ComponentIndustrial</li>
            <li>ComponentIndustrial</li>
            <li>ComponentIndustrial</li>
            <li>ComponentIndustrial</li>
            <li>ComponentIndustrial</li>
            <li>ComponentIndustrial</li>
            <li>ComponentIndustrial</li>
            <li>ComponentIndustrial</li>
            <li>ChunkSlagSteel</li>
            <li>ChunkSlagSteel</li>
            <li>ChunkSlagSteel</li>
            <li>ChunkSlagSteel</li>
          </items>
        </li>

        <!-- Ground tile, close enough to caravan to. -->
        <li Class="QuestNode_GetSiteTile">
          <storeAs>siteTile</storeAs>
          <preferCloserTiles>true</preferCloserTiles>
        </li>

        <!-- Opposition: whatever the engine gives cheapest, and thin. -->
        <li Class="QuestNode_ViolentQuestsAllowed">
          <node Class="QuestNode_Set">
            <name>siteThreatChance</name>
            <value>0.4</value>
          </node>
          <elseNode Class="QuestNode_Set">
            <name>siteThreatChance</name>
            <value>0</value>
          </elseNode>
        </li>

        <li Class="QuestNode_GetSitePartDefsByTagsAndFaction">
          <storeAs>sitePartDefs</storeAs>
          <storeFactionAs>siteFaction</storeFactionAs>
          <sitePartsTags>
            <li>
              <tag>ItemStash</tag>
            </li>
            <li>
              <tag>ItemStashQuestThreat</tag>
              <chance>$siteThreatChance</chance>
            </li>
          </sitePartsTags>
        </li>

        <li Class="QuestNode_GetDefaultSitePartsParams">
          <tile>$siteTile</tile>
          <faction>$siteFaction</faction>
          <sitePartDefs>$sitePartDefs</sitePartDefs>
          <storeSitePartsParamsAs>sitePartsParams</storeSitePartsParamsAs>
        </li>

        <li Class="QuestNode_SubScript">
          <def>Util_GenerateSite</def>
        </li>

        <li Class="QuestNode_SpawnWorldObjects">
          <worldObjects>$site</worldObjects>
        </li>

        <!--
          Expiry: a rival clan planted their marker first. No penalty and no
          goodwill change - the only loss is the opportunity. Disabled the moment
          the player generates the site map, so it can never race the success
          path below.
        -->
        <li Class="QuestNode_WorldObjectTimeout">
          <worldObject>$site</worldObject>
          <isQuestTimeout>true</isQuestTimeout>
          <delayTicks>$(randInt(10,18)*60000)</delayTicks>
          <inSignalDisable>site.MapGenerated</inSignalDisable>
          <node Class="QuestNode_Sequence">
            <nodes>
              <li Class="QuestNode_Letter">
                <label>Quest expired: [resolvedQuestName]</label>
                <text>Someone else's marker is standing in it. By the time your people crest the ridge there is nothing left worth the walk back — stripped to the frame, and the frame is spoken for.\n\nThey were closer. That is the whole of it.</text>
              </li>
              <li Class="QuestNode_End">
                <outcome>Fail</outcome>
              </li>
            </nodes>
          </node>
        </li>

        <!--
          Success: armed only after the player has actually been to the wreck,
          then fires when they leave and the site map is removed.
        -->
        <li Class="QuestNode_SignalActivable">
          <inSignal>site.MapRemoved</inSignal>
          <inSignalEnable>site.MapGenerated</inSignalEnable>
          <node Class="QuestNode_Sequence">
            <nodes>
              <li Class="QuestNode_Letter">
                <label>Quest completed</label>
                <letterDef>PositiveEvent</letterDef>
                <text>The marker stands. What was in the hull is on the sled and moving.</text>
              </li>
              <li Class="QuestNode_End">
                <outcome>Success</outcome>
              </li>
            </nodes>
          </node>
        </li>

      </nodes>
    </root>
  </QuestScriptDef>

</Defs>
